"""Identification of listens as probabilistic record linkage: which written work (and which recording) is each listen?

Steps: `query` reads what each listen says about itself (tags, folder name, chosen fields, runtime) as several *readings*; `candidates` finds possible works in the local Open Library and Audible indexes and joins the two into work clusters (an Open Library work plus the Audible recordings of it); `compare` turns each (listen, work) pair into a vector of discrete agreement levels; `model` is a Fellegi-Sunter model fitted by EM (semi-supervised: known answers are clamped) that gives each candidate a posterior probability, including the probability that the listen is none of them; `apply` writes the answer to the listen as `match` listen-parts. See docs/listen-identification.md."""
